      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/south-point-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community’s name likely comes from its geographic position near the Rio Grande’s southernmost bend.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/south-point-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "South Point lies at 25°52′12″N 97°23′00″W, just north and west of the river’s bend that marks Texas’s southernmost point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Point%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town is roughly nine miles east of Brownsville’s city center, placing it close to the U.S.–Mexico border.",
